    "body": "**O/I/T:**\n- Objective: the freeze gate cannot see an ANNOTATION change behind an approved tool, although the MCP `tools/list` `inputSchema` publishes annotations as the parameter `type` \u2014 the same blindness #4192 reports for parameter defaults, and the same code path.\n- Indicators: a tool's annotation changed in the source with the baseline untouched reds the required `surface-guard` job; the fingerprint cell covers `__defaults__`, `__kwdefaults__` AND `__annotations__`.\n- Targets: 0 annotations changes that pass the gate; 1 test that fails without the fix.\n\n**Team:** unknown (lane:c7-instrumentation)\n**Complexity:** standard\n\n**Epic:** standalone\n**Research:** none\n**Depends on:** none\n**Related:** #4192, #4170, #4180\n**Components:** tools/surface-guard.py, tools/surface_manifest.py, config/surface-manifest.yml\n\n### Context\n\n`_code_digest` digests a tool's code object (bytecode, names, constants). A function's\n`__annotations__` is **not** in its code object \u2014 it is built by the `def` statement's\n`MAKE_FUNCTION`/`SETUP_ANNOTATIONS` in the DEFINING module's code object \u2014 and the MCP\n`inputSchema` for each tool is derived from it. Measured on `origin/main` at\n`90f61ec59` (2026-10-10):\n\n```\n$ python -c \"from tortoise import mcp_server; ...\"   # tools/list schema for tortoise_search\n\"entity_type\": {\"default\": \"point\", \"type\": \"string\"}     # <- type = the annotation\n```\n\nand all 82 served tool functions carry annotations (`q: str | None` \u2192 `anyOf [string, null]`),\nso `q: str` \u2192 `q: int` changes what every agent is told to pass while the recorded\n`served_from` fingerprint stays byte-identical (the code object does not change).\n\nThis is the same defect class as #4192 (parameter defaults) and #4180 (constants), found by\nre-measuring the identity while fixing #4192. It is fixed together with #4192 by the per-row\n`served_attributes` cell, which hashes `__defaults__`, `__kwdefaults__` and `__annotations__`\n\u2014 recorded here so the finding survives independently of that PR.\n\n### Research Needed\nNone \u2014 the mechanism and the measurement are in the PR that closes this.\n\n### Complexity (domain-aware)\n| Domain | Rating | Rationale |\n|--------|--------|-----------|\n| Config | standard | the freeze artifact's schema gains a derived cell; CI gates and the pinned-guard interaction must hold |\n| Architecture | low | one fingerprint function, mirrored in two tools |\n\n### Fractal Fields\n- **Level:** task\n- **OIT:** see above \u2014 populated at creation\n- **E2E:** covered by the PR's `tests/test_surface_manifest.py` cases (unit + guard integration + `check` end-to-end)\n- **Verification:** tests/test_surface_manifest.py (118 passed), tests/test_surface_guard_pin_4606.py (7 passed)\n- **Wiring:** `build_doc` \u2192 `config/surface-manifest.yml` \u2192 `check`; guard row comparison\n",
